  "live_records": {
    "q-346659": {
      "dom_id": "step-q346659",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Evaluate the indicator function\n$1[9\\in \\{1,2,3,5\\}].$",
      "worked_solution": "The indicator function $1[P]$ equals $1$ if the predicate $P$ is true and $0$ if $P$ is false.\n\n$$\n1[P]=\\{\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is true}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is false}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, the predicate is $9\\in \\{1,2,3,5\\}.$ Since $9$ is not an element of the set $\\{1,2,3,5\\},$ the predicate is false. Therefore,\n\n$$\n1[9\\in \\{1,2,3,5\\}]=0.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
