    "q-351129": {
      "dom_id": "step-q351129",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Let $E=\\{0,4,8,12\\}.$ Which of the following is equivalent to $1[10\\in E]?$",
      "worked_solution": "The indicator function $1[P]$ equals $1$ if the predicate $P$ is true and $0$ if $P$ is false.\n\n$$\n1[P]=\\{\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is true}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is false}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the indicator function ${1}_{A}(x)$ of a set $A$ equals $1$ if $x\\in A$ and $0$ if $x\\notin A.$ This can be written using Iverson bracket notation as\n\n$$\n{1}_{A}(x)=1[x\\in A].\n$$\n\nHere, the Iverson bracket expression $1[10\\in E]$ has $x=10$ and $A=E.$ Therefore, converting back to set indicator notation, we have\n\n$$\n1[10\\in E]={1}_{E}(10).\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
