    "q-351130": {
      "dom_id": "step-q351130",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Let $F=\\{3,6,9,15\\}.$ Which of the following is equivalent to $1[8\\in F]?$",
      "worked_solution": "The indicator function $1[P]$ equals $1$ if the predicate $P$ is true and $0$ if $P$ is false.\n\n$$\n1[P]=\\{\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is true}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is false}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the indicator function ${1}_{A}(x)$ of a set $A$ equals $1$ if $x\\in A$ and $0$ if $x\\notin A.$ This can be written using Iverson bracket notation as\n\n$$\n{1}_{A}(x)=1[x\\in A].\n$$\n\nHere, the Iverson bracket expression $1[8\\in F]$ has $x=8$ and $A=F.$ Therefore, converting back to set indicator notation, we have\n\n$$\n1[8\\in F]={1}_{F}(8).\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-351130-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{1}_{8}(3)",
              "html": "<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"116\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-msub><mjx-texatom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-b\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D7CF TEX-B\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-texatom><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.15em;\"><mjx-texatom size=\"s\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c38\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-texatom></mjx-script></mjx-msub><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c28\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c29\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn mathvariant=\"bold\">1</mn></mrow><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>8</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>"
            },
            {
