    "q-346661": {
      "dom_id": "step-q346661",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Let $B=\\{2,4,6,8\\}.$ Which of the following is equivalent to ${1}_{B}(4)?$",
      "worked_solution": "The indicator function $1[P]$ equals $1$ if the predicate $P$ is true and $0$ if $P$ is false.\n\n$$\n1[P]=\\{\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is true}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is false}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the indicator function ${1}_{B}(x)$ of a set $B$ equals $1$ if $x\\in B$ and $0$ if $x\\notin B.$ This can be written using Iverson bracket notation as\n\n$$\n{1}_{B}(x)=1[x\\in B].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{1}_{B}(4)=1[4\\in B]=1[4\\in \\{2,4,6,8\\}].\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
