      "dom_id": "step-q346669",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "$$\n{x}_{1}=-3,\\,{x}_{2}=6,\\,{x}_{3}=0,\\,{x}_{4}=2,\\,{x}_{5}=-1\n$$\n\nGiven the values ${x}_{1},\\,{x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3},\\,{x}_{4},\\,{x}_{5}$ above, we have\n\n${\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}1[{x}_{i}>0]\\cdot {x}_{i}=$ {{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The indicator function $1[P]$ equals $1$ if the predicate $P$ is true and $0$ if $P$ is false.\n\n$$\n1[P]=\\{\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is true}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is false}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe expression $1[{x}_{i}>0]\\cdot {x}_{i}$ equals ${x}_{i}$ when ${x}_{i}>0$ and equals $0$ otherwise. Thus, the sum \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}1[{x}_{i}>0]\\cdot {x}_{i}\n$$\n\nadds up only the positive values.\n\nWe evaluate the indicator function for each ${x}_{i}:$\n\n- $1[{x}_{1}>0]=1[-3>0]=0$\n\n- $1[{x}_{2}>0]=1[6>0]=1$\n\n- $1[{x}_{3}>0]=1[0>0]=0$\n\n- $1[{x}_{4}>0]=1[2>0]=1$\n\n- $1[{x}_{5}>0]=1[-1>0]=0$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}1[{x}_{i}>0]\\cdot {x}_{i} & =0\\cdot (-3)+1\\cdot 6+0\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 2+0\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =0+6+0+2+0 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
