    "q-347932": {
      "dom_id": "step-q347932",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "$$\n{x}_{1}=-3,\\,{x}_{2}=1,\\,{x}_{3}=6,\\,{x}_{4}=-2,\\,{x}_{5}=0\n$$\n\nGiven the values ${x}_{1},\\,{x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3},\\,{x}_{4},\\,{x}_{5}$ above, we have\n\n${\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}1[{x}_{i}\\ge 0]\\cdot ({x}_{i}-1)+1[{x}_{i}<0]\\cdot 2=$ {{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The indicator function $1[P]$ equals $1$ if the predicate $P$ is true and $0$ if $P$ is false.\n\n$$\n1[P]=\\{\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is true}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is false}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe expression $1[{x}_{i}\\ge 0]\\cdot ({x}_{i}-1)+1[{x}_{i}<0]\\cdot 2$ equals ${x}_{i}-1$ when ${x}_{i}\\ge 0$ and equals $2$ when ${x}_{i}<0.$ Thus, the sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}1[{x}_{i}\\ge 0]\\cdot ({x}_{i}-1)+1[{x}_{i}<0]\\cdot 2\n$$\n\nadds ${x}_{i}-1$ for nonnegative values and $2$ for negative values.\n\nWe evaluate the indicator function for each ${x}_{i}:$\n\n- $1[{x}_{1}\\ge 0]=1[-3\\ge 0]=0,$ $1[{x}_{1}<0]=1$\n\n- $1[{x}_{2}\\ge 0]=1[1\\ge 0]=1,$ $1[{x}_{2}<0]=0$\n\n- $1[{x}_{3}\\ge 0]=1[6\\ge 0]=1,$ $1[{x}_{3}<0]=0$\n\n- $1[{x}_{4}\\ge 0]=1[-2\\ge 0]=0,$ $1[{x}_{4}<0]=1$\n\n- $1[{x}_{5}\\ge 0]=1[0\\ge 0]=1,$ $1[{x}_{5}<0]=0$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}1[{x}_{i}\\ge 0]\\cdot ({x}_{i}-1)+1[{x}_{i}<0]\\cdot 2 & =2+(1-1)+(6-1)+2+(0-1) \\\\  & =2+0+5+2-1 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
